ncluded; if 'greater than or equal', both included. But the rule says 'higher than', so strictly, not included. So B has no probable outcomes. Then average for B is undefined or 0. Thus, the reason would prefer A. So the reason can be applied with a strict interpretation, leading to a preference for A due to having a single certain outcome that qualifies as probable (if we allow p ≥ 1/n), while B’s outcomes do not (p = 50% not > 50%).",
